            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.342,
            0.314,
            0.367
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.376,
            0.755,
            0.396
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the median of onion prices in Yahapur and Wahapur."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.401,
            0.847,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Sanskruti asked her class how many domestic animals and pets each had at home. Some of the students were absent. The data values are 0, 1, 0, 4, 8, 0, 0, 2, 1, 1, 5, 3, 4, 0, 0, —, 10, 25, 2, — , 2, 4. Find the mean and median. How would you describe this data?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.482,
            0.849,
            0.618
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Rintu takes care of a date-palm tree farm in Habra. The heights of the trees (in feet) in his farm are given as: 50, 45, 43, 52, 61, 63, 46, 55, 60, 55, 59, 56, 56, 49, 54, 65, 66, 51, 44, 58, 60, 54, 52, 57, 61, 62, 60, 60, 67. Fill the dot plot, and mark the mean and median. How would you describe the heights of these palm trees? Can you think of quicker ways to find the mean? How many trees are shorter than the average height?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.625,
            0.844,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "chart_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.154,
                0.625,
                0.844,
                0.701
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_chart_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.707,
            0.846,
            0.747
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. The daily water usage from a tap was measured. The usage in liters for the first few days are: 5.6, 8, 3.09, 12.9, 6.5, 12.1, 11.3, 20.5, 7.4."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.751,
            0.846,
            0.792
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) Can the mean or median daily usage lie between 25 and 30? Justify your claim using the meaning of mean and median."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.795,
            0.847,
            0.835
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) Can the mean or median be lesser than the minimum value or greater than the maximum value in a data?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.839,
            0.847,
            0.88
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. The weights of a few newborn babies are given in kgs. Fill the dot plot provided below. Analyse and compare this data."
            }
          ]
        },
